    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b4494c1e_54ade0ca",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 3276,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-30T19:22:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The thrust of this sentence is that the onAvailable() ceases to track or otherwise care about the previous onAvailable() network the moment this is invoked. If there\u0027s a way to emphasize that I think it would be good. See above comment to further clarify that this sentence only applies to requestNetwork() behavior.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3275,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 3276,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "09230250de3fda7a4caa362eb236a8331f7966ef",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c7ae33d7_da2d403c",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 3276,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-02T05:37:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not completely sure what you mean, because onAvailable() does not track anything, it\u0027s just a function call. Maybe you mean the callback is only providing information about the last available network ? I added a sentence to this effect, see if you like it.",
      "parentUuid": "b4494c1e_54ade0ca",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3275,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 3276,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "09230250de3fda7a4caa362eb236a8331f7966ef",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b00cd97_6bcec454",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 3296,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-30T19:22:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "is onLost() called when a network is *expected* to be lost (but could somehow survive), or is it only called when a network is guaranteed to be lost (providing a grace period)? If it\u0027s \"expected\" then I\u0027d suggest clarifying.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3296,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 3296,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "09230250de3fda7a4caa362eb236a8331f7966ef",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8556fa7e_dc5cad5c",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 3296,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-02T05:37:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No guarantees on either.\n\nThe platform wants to tell apps this network should be treated as if it\u0027s going to be lost soon. Whether the platform intends and/or expects at this point to lose it, we refuse to make any commitment about.\n\nDo you have any better idea of wording ?",
      "parentUuid": "0b00cd97_6bcec454",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3296,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 3296,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "09230250de3fda7a4caa362eb236a8331f7966ef",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4edeb70d_1b00ac64",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 3304,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-30T19:22:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "suggest \"within the callback: the behavior of this is undefined (due to potential race conditions).\"\n\nDevelopers are familiar with the concept of UBI, so leveraging that kind of terminology makes sense. I\u0027d like to start seeing it adopted in more places.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3303,
        "startChar": 96,
        "endLine": 3304,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "09230250de3fda7a4caa362eb236a8331f7966ef",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9816456_1d8cb7e9",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 3304,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-02T05:37:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "UBI has a pretty strict meaning in many contexts and I don\u0027t think this is it. This is guaranteed not to make demons fly out of you nose. That\u0027s why I don\u0027t like too much this wording here.\n\nUsed the wording in onLost, as I think it\u0027s the best we have.",
      "parentUuid": "4edeb70d_1b00ac64",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3303,
        "startChar": 96,
        "endLine": 3304,
        "endChar": 61
      },
