      "writtenOn": "2019-10-02T05:37:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here is the scenario.\n• The device has the \"mobile data always on\" setting turned off\n• No app is requesting mobile data\n• The device is currently connected to an Ethernet network\nIn this context, suppose an app with the appropriate set of permissions wants to connect specifically to a cellular network for its own purposes. Maybe it\u0027s a carrier app that wants to do something on its network or something.\n\nThe app will use requestNetwork() with a request for TRANSPORT_CELLULAR and NET_CAPABILITY_INTERNET. This *will* bring up a cellular network if possible. If the user turned off mobile data, it\u0027s not possible.\n\nWould you reword this in any way to clarify ?",
